---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Lincoln Egress Windows"
  description="The terms you accept by using this site, and the line between what we do and what the contractor who takes your job does."
  canonical="https://lincolnegresswindows.com/terms/"
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://lincolnegresswindows.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Terms of Service", "item": "https://lincolnegresswindows.com/terms/"}]}</script>
<style is:global>
  .legal { max-width: 780px; }
  .legal h2 { font-family: 'Nunito Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 1.45rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0A3D5C; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.7rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .legal p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: #4A5A66; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .legal li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: #4A5A66; margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .legal strong { color: #2B3A44; font-weight: 700; }
  .legal a { color: #1273A8; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .legal a:hover { color: #0C5680; }
</style>
</Fragment>

<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="max-width:1220px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px 24px;">
  <ol style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;gap:8px;font-size:13px;color:#8A9AA5;">
    <li><a href="/" style="color:#1273A8;text-decoration:none;">Home</a></li>
    <li>/</li>
    <li style="color:#5A6B76;">Terms of Service</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0A3D5C 0%,#1273A8 100%);padding:60px 24px 68px;">
  <div style="max-width:1220px;margin:0 auto;">
    <h1 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,42px);font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:620px;margin:0;">The terms you accept by using this site, and the line between what we do and what the contractor who takes your job does.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:56px 24px 76px;">
  <div style="max-width:1220px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="legal">

      <p>These terms govern your use of lincolnegresswindows.com. By using the site or calling a number published on it, you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.</p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>Lincoln Egress Windows is a referral service. We publish information about egress windows in Lincoln and southeast Nebraska and connect callers with independent contractors. <strong>We are not an egress window contractor.</strong> We do not cut foundations, install windows, dig wells, employ crews, or pull permits, and we may be compensated when you call. Our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> sets this out in full.</p>

      <h2>We are not a party to your agreement with a contractor</h2>
      <p>Any work you arrange is a contract between you and the contractor. That includes the price, the scope, the schedule, the permit, the structural approach, the restoration, and any dispute that follows. We do not set prices, supervise work, inspect results, hold the contractor's insurance, or guarantee performance.</p>
      <p>You are responsible for satisfying yourself as to a contractor's licensing, insurance, workers' compensation coverage, and competence before work begins. Our <a href="/blog/hiring-egress-window-contractor-checklist/">contractor hiring checklist</a> explains how to verify each of these.</p>

      <h2>Information, not advice</h2>
      <p>Content on this site is general information. It is not engineering, structural, legal, insurance, or financial advice, and it is not a substitute for a licensed contractor or engineer assessing your specific foundation.</p>
      <p>Code figures published here — including the <strong>5.7 square foot</strong> net clear opening, the <strong>24 inch</strong> and <strong>20 inch</strong> minimums, the <strong>44 inch</strong> maximum sill height, and window well dimensions — reflect the International Residential Code as generally adopted. Adoption, amendment, and enforcement differ between Lincoln-Lancaster County and the jurisdictions covering Waverly, Hickman, Ashland, Crete, Seward, and Beatrice, and they change over time. Confirm the requirements with the office that will issue your permit before relying on anything here.</p>
      <p>Prices published here are general ranges for the Lincoln area, offered so you can budget and recognise an outlier. They are not quotes, offers, or commitments, and the contractor who inspects your property sets the actual price.</p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>Nothing on this site is an emergency service. Same-day and 24/7 availability depend on provider participation, location, technician availability, and demand, and are not guaranteed. If you have an active water or electrical hazard in a basement, address that first and do not wait on a contractor.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not submit false information or another person's details through the contact form.</li>
        <li>Do not use the site to harass, or to send automated or bulk enquiries.</li>
        <li>Do not scrape, copy, or republish site content without permission.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to interfere with the site's operation or security.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The text, layout, and design of this site are ours and are protected by copyright. You may read, print, and share pages for your own use. Republishing content, in whole or substantial part, requires our written permission.</p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>We link to outside resources — city and county building departments, code bodies, manufacturers — because they are useful. We do not control them and are not responsible for their content or their practices.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>The site is provided "as is". We work to keep it accurate and current, but we do not warrant that it is free of errors or omissions, that it will be available uninterrupted, or that any particular contractor will be available to you.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by Nebraska law, Lincoln Egress Windows is not liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of this site, from information published on it, or from work performed by a contractor you were connected with. Claims relating to the work itself — including structural damage, water intrusion, failed inspection, or defective installation — lie against the contractor who performed it.</p>
      <p>Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>How we handle your information, including the fact that calls are tracked and may be recorded, is set out in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may revise these terms. The version published here at the time you use the site is the one that applies.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Nebraska.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:info@lincolnegresswindows.com">info@lincolnegresswindows.com</a>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem;font-size:14px;color:#8A9AA5;">Last updated: 20 August 2026</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
